# lib.mcu, Pico SDK

This platform's implementation of the portable mm.mcu interface. It registers a
Platform subclass at static initialisation, so an executable that links it answers
through Pico SDK and one that does not answers Unsupported.

It names the pico-sdk library, which is true and load-bearing: the definitions it
calls come from the adapter that library's bridge compiles, and naming it is what
makes this module available only in a lane whose selected SDK names pico-sdk. In
any other lane it is a skipped unavailable target, so nothing can link a
registration whose adapter is absent.

The C is all below this module: the SDK adapter the bridge compiles, reached
through a private ABI and its linkage shim. An application names lib.mcu in its
manifest and mm.mcu in its source, which is what keeps the source portable while
the implementation stays here.
